{
  "schema_version": "2",
  "description": "Ovarian tumor histology alias table used by _clean_histology_for_query (src/omgs/products/omgs/mdt_core/servers/evidence_retrieval.py). Surface forms in Chinese (aliases_zh) and English abbreviations (aliases_en) found in pathology reports and clinical notes are mapped to NCCN-canonical English phrases used to seed guideline / PubMed RAG queries.",
  "sources": [
    "WHO Classification of Female Genital Tumours, 5th edition (2020) — https://whobluebooks.iarc.who.int/structures/female-genital-tumours/",
    "NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Ovarian Cancer, including Fallopian Tube Cancer and Primary Peritoneal Cancer (consolidated guideline covering Epithelial Ovarian, Less Common Ovarian Cancers, Malignant Germ Cell Tumors, Malignant Sex Cord-Stromal Tumors, and Small Cell Carcinoma of the Ovary)"
  ],
  "usage_notes": [
    "Matching is longest-alias-first: “高级别浆液性癌” wins over the shorter backstop “浆液性癌”.",
    "aliases_zh matches are case-sensitive, substring over the raw input.",
    "aliases_en matches are case-insensitive to accept HGSC / hgsc / HgSc equally.",
    "canonical_en is used verbatim inside the RAG query string; lower-case wording aligns with typical NCCN / PubMed abstract casing.",
    "english_term_whitelist drives the fallback ASCII-only branch: if an input already contains one of these, we strip non-ASCII instead of returning empty."
  ],
